  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNAMID, Sydsudan</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations-African Union Hybrid Operation in Darfur. The main task is to protect civilians and to promote and mediate peace between the parts of the conflict. The activities of Individual Police Officers (IPOs) mostly focus on monitoring, mentoring and building the capacity of local Police, and supporting community-oriented policing undertakings in Darfur by building and improving the capacity of Community Policing Volunteers and Community Safety Committees in IDP Camps. Through these activities, IPOs bridge the gap between the local Police and IDPs, especially in areas where there is deep mistrust between the two sides. IPOs also contribute to enhance early warning for the mission through interaction with the community and engage in confidence building patrol.</narrative>
  </description>
